    "dynamic_faq_8AUh7M": {
      "type": "dynamic-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_nCTWbR": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does the Lawn Mower Pro Module include the Core?",
            "answer": "<p>No. This is the module itself, engineered to attach to a Yarbo Core you already own or purchase alongside it. Confirm your configuration before checkout.<br/><br/></p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_69jhiF": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What separates the Pro from the standard mower module?",
            "answer": "<p>Power, and what that power makes possible. Dual 300W motors deliver up to 2,500 watts of peak output, roughly double the standard module, purpose-built for properties where grass doesn't always cooperate.<br/><br/></p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_8KCdGW": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it perform on thick or overgrown grass?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. That is precisely the condition the Pro was engineered to solve. Where standard mowers hesitate on dense turf or grass left too long, the added motor power carries through without loss of cut quality.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_EcA6Mx": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much ground can it cover?",
            "answer": "<p>Up to 6 acres, sized for large residential properties and commercial applications alike, not a scaled-up version of a small-yard machine.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_BQYmLz": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does it handle slopes and uneven terrain?",
            "answer": "<p>The Core's tracked drive system, to which the Pro module attaches, is rated for grades up to 70 percent, or 35 degrees. Uneven ground and rolling terrain are within its intended operating range.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_JjXiyk": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between the standard discs and the straight blades?",
            "answer": "<p>The standard reinforced discs handle everyday mowing. The optional SK85 high-carbon steel straight blades, sometimes labeled \"mulching blades\" in Yarbo's own materials, are for a finer, more deliberate finish, cutting grass into smaller clippings that break down faster and return nutrients to the lawn, with less frequent maintenance required.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_JxkamV": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What kind of support do I get after purchase?",
            "answer": "<p>Ownership here means more than a warranty. Yard Automation Pros pairs Yarbo’s 2 year manufacturer warranty on defective parts with our own US based support team, on hand for mapping, setup, and the seasonal details that keep an estate running the way it should.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
